---
// PILLAR — Educational Leader. The earliest chronological pillar, so it sits
// before Premier Leadership.
//
// ENTRANCE — TREATMENT A, the hairline head. A Smoked Slate rule runs from the
// kicker across to the live margin and terminates on the section numeral; the
// role line drops beneath it. About above opens on a drop cap and Premier
// below opens on a display numeral, so neither neighbour is matched.
//
// COLUMN WINDOW — B, the WIDE one: columns 2-7, a column left of the page
// default. This is the section with the most body copy on the page and it is
// the one that can carry being pulled toward the trim.
//
// No image, deliberately, and it stays that way — CONTEXT.md's photography
// rule keeps photographs out of adjacent sections and this is the section
// nominated to go without. The live margin carries the section instead.
//
// Contact: the district WEBSITE is published; her district EMAIL is not. That
// address is her public-school-district employer address and it does not
// belong on a commercial consulting page. Final client decision, not a
// placeholder. The address itself is deliberately not written anywhere in
// this tree, comments included, so a grep for it stays clean.
//
// NO HAND-SET grid-column ANYWHERE IN THIS FILE. Every placement is a
// collapse-aware primitive from global.css. See the collapse table there.
---

<section class="education spread" id="sec-education">
  <!-- TREATMENT A. The <h2> is the kicker, so the element naming the section
       is still the element the folio labels — unchanged by the outdent. -->
  <div class="section-head section-head--wide col-rule-wide row-1">
    <h2 class="kicker">Educational Leader</h2>
    <span class="head-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="section-numeral section-numeral--head" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
    <p class="role">Alternative Education High School Principal</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Edge 2 of 3: the lede sits on the window's body edge, column 2. -->
  <p class="lede col-body-wide row-2">Education should not simply require students to fit into systems; strong systems must also be willing to evolve to meet the needs of the students they serve.</p>

  <!-- Edge 3 of 3: the paragraphs indent one column in, to column 3. -->
  <div class="body-copy col-indent-wide row-3">
    <!-- Paragraph 1 ends at "traditional measures." The rest of the client's
         sentence is detached upward into the lede above and is not repeated. -->
    <p>For more than two decades, Dr.&nbsp;Syreeta McClain has dedicated her career to seeing possibility in young people&mdash;especially those whose potential may not always be recognized through traditional measures.</p>
    <p>Her expertise in customized high school programming, alternative education, student engagement, and leadership has allowed her to create pathways for students navigating complex academic and life circumstances. Through innovation, technology, collaboration, compassion, and unwavering advocacy, Dr.&nbsp;McClain works to build educational environments where students are seen, supported, challenged, and prepared for what comes next.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- A CODA, not a pull quote: there is exactly one pull quote on this page
       and it is the chapter break. It steps back OUT to the lede's edge
       rather than staying on the body indent — the staircase run in reverse
       is what sets it apart, so it needs no rule and no ornament. -->
  <p class="coda col-body-wide row-4">At the heart of her leadership is a simple belief: meet students where they are, without losing sight of where they are capable of going.</p>

  <!-- Live margin. Last in source order so that when the margin collapses at
       1280 it falls inline in reading order, after the copy rather than
       before it. Positioned by grid, never by position:absolute — a screen
       reader meets the district link where it belongs in the text. -->
  <aside class="margin-block col-margin row-3">
    <p class="margin-label">District</p>
    <a class="margin-link" href="https://www.ucvts.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ucvts.org</a>
  </aside>
</section>

<style>
  /* RHYTHM: standard. Assigned per section, never one repeating gap. */
  .education{ padding-top: var(--vr-standard); }

  /* Intermediate scale — ~1.9x the body, well under the lede, so it is
     plainly larger than the paragraphs and plainly smaller than the display
     line. The OPEN step above it. That step is the chapter break's own, but
     the break spends it TWICE (margin + padding), so it stays the largest gap
     on the page by roughly 2x and this does not compete with it. */
  .coda{
    margin: var(--vr-open) 0 0;
    max-width: 34ch;
    font-family: var(--display);
    /* Coda tier — opsz 48, wght 360, SOFT 45, WONK 0. */
    font-variation-settings: var(--fx-coda);
    font-weight: 360;
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.1vw, 30px);
    line-height: 1.42;
    letter-spacing: -0.008em;
    color: var(--obsidian);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1024px){
    .coda{ max-width: none; }
  }
</style>
